course: dictionary
lesson: 8172
title: Same word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. Look at the words around the word. They are the clues. Resin is one of these words.
explain: Resin is a thick, sticky liquid that comes out of some trees, especially pine trees. «Amber is tree resin that hardened over millions of years; insects stuck in the sticky resin were sealed in.» The clues sticky and sealed in tell you resin traps things, and it goes hard over time.
explain: Resin can also be man-made. «Epoxy resin» is a kind of plastic that is poured as a liquid and sets hard, and people use it for glue, models and jewellery. So resin can mean tree gum or a factory plastic. Check the clues to find which one fits.
fact: Resin is a thick, sticky liquid that comes out of some trees, especially pine trees.
fact: Resin protects a tree when its bark is hurt, because it oozes out and seals the wound.
fact: Resin becomes hard over time, and very old hardened resin can be a fossil called amber.
fact: «Rosin» is hardened pine resin that violinists rub on their bows so the hair grips the strings.
fact: «Epoxy resin» is a man-made plastic that is poured as a liquid and sets hard.
exercise: «Amber is tree resin that hardened over millions of years.» What does resin mean here? | *A sticky liquid from a tree that goes hard | A type of stone dug from the sea | A cold wind in winter | A kind of paint for walls
exercise: «Epoxy resin» is used for jewellery and models. What kind of material is epoxy resin? | A metal from a mine | A dried flower | *A man-made plastic that sets hard | A soft cloth
exercise: Violinists rub «rosin» on their bows. Where does rosin come from? | Horsehair | Sea salt | *Hardened pine resin | Sheep wool
test: «Insects stuck in the sticky resin were sealed in.» Which word tells you resin is sticky? | Were | *Sticky | Sealed | Insects
test: A tree oozes resin when its bark is hurt. Why does it do this? | To make its leaves grow faster | *To protect the wounded bark | To make the tree taller | To feed the birds
exam: Does the word resin always mean tree gum? | Only in cold countries | *No, epoxy resin is a man-made plastic, so the context decides | Yes, always | Only in science lessons
